:PNLGRP.
.*
:HELP name='PINGPORT/ALL'.
:IMHELP name=PINGPORT.
:IMHELP name='PINGPORT/HOST    '.
:IMHELP name='PINGPORT/PORT    '.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für den Befehl
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='PINGPORT'.
Ping with Port (PINGPORT) - Help
:P.
The Verify TCP/IP Connection with Port (PINGPORT) command tests the
connectivity between a system and the remote system and port specified
at the command line.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort HOST
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PINGPORT/HOST      '.
Host name or IP address - Help
:XH3.Host name or IP address (HOST)
:P.
Specifies the remote system name of the host with which
the Verify TCP/IP operation takes place.  To be
successful, the name must be valid, and the remote system
must be able to communicate with the local system.  Also
there must be a listener running on the remote system and
listening on the port specified at the :HP2.PORT:EHP2. parameter.
:P.
In order to test the connection the command attempts to open a
connection to the remote system and port. It then immediately
closes the connection. It does not send any data to the remote
system.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the DNS name or IP address of the remote system to be
verified.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort PORT
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PINGPORT/PORT      '.
Port number - Help
:XH3.Port number (PORT)
:P.
Specify the port number of the listener running on the remote system.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.port-number:EPV.
:PD.Specify the port number of the listener that is running on
the remote system.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*====================================================================
.*  Textbausteine, die an mehreren Stellen im Hilfetext
.*  verwendet werden.
.*====================================================================

.*=====================================
.*  Erforderlicher Parameter
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/REQPARM'.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
:EHELP.

.*=====================================
.*  Optionaler Parameter
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
This is an optional parameter.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
:EHELP.

.*=====================================
.*  Werteliste
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/VALUES'.
:P.
The possible values are:
:EHELP.
.*
:EPNLGRP.
